%N A399050 Square array A(n,k), n >= 1, k >= 0, read by antidiagonals downwards, where A(n,k) = lcm(n, n+1, ..., n+k).
%C A399050 The function M(n,k) in Erdős Problem 677 is given by M(n,k) = A(n+1,k-1), for n >= 1 and k >= 1.
%H A399050 Thomas F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/677">Erdős Problem 677</a>, Erdős Problems.
%e A399050 Square array begins:
%e A399050   1,  2,   6,  12,   60,    60,   420, ...
%e A399050   2,  6,  12,  60,   60,   420,   840, ...
%e A399050   3, 12,  60,  60,  420,   840,  2520, ...
%e A399050   4, 20,  60, 420,  840,  2520,  2520, ...
%e A399050   5, 30, 210, 840, 2520,  2520, 27720, ...
%e A399050   6, 42, 168, 504, 2520, 27720, 27720, ...
%e A399050   ...
%o A399050 (PARI) a(n, k) = lcm(vector(k+1, j, n+j-1));
%Y A399050 Columns k=0..4 give A000027, A002378, A033931, 12*A067047, 60*A067048.
%Y A399050 Row n=1 gives A003418(k+1).
%Y A399050 Cf. A067049.
%K A399050 nonn,tabl,new
%O A399050 1,2
